## Implementation

### Web (Web Audio API)
```
AudioContext → GainNode (master) → destination
                ├── GainNode (sfx)   → SFX buffers
                └── GainNode (music) → Music buffer
```
- Preload all SFX as AudioBuffers on game init
- Create new AudioBufferSourceNode per play (they're one-shot)
- Master volume: `1.0`, SFX: `0.8`, Music: `0.5` (defaults, tunable via settings)
- Resume AudioContext on first user interaction (Chrome autoplay policy)

### Unity
- Audio Sources on dedicated AudioManager GameObject
- SFX via `AudioSource.PlayOneShot()` (pooled, max 8 concurrent)
- Music via separate looping AudioSource with crossfade

### Roblox
- SoundService for global sounds
- Sound objects parented to parts for spatial audio
- SoundGroup for volume categories (SFX, Music, UI)

